// Bank / card SMS. ALL TEXT IS FABRICATED — no real account numbers, no real
// people, no real merchant tied to anyone. Masks (4471/8802/3319/1207/6650) and
// references are obviously synthetic; merchants are invented (TESTMART,
// SAMPLECAFE, QUICKCART, METROFUEL, TESTSTREAM).
//
// `expect` is PRODUCT GROUND TRUTH: what a correct agent must do once extraction
// exists. Per architecture §3.1 stage 8 a model extraction is confirm-gated, so
// the ground truth for a parseable bank SMS is `draft`, never `write`.
//
// With the default `null` provider there is no recipe cache and no model, so the
// cascade has nothing behind the grammar's (correct) refusal and every
// TRANSACTIONAL SMS lands on ignore/not_parseable. Those are marked
// expectedFailure — the bucket is the headline measurement of what a model buys.
{"id":"sms-hdfc-upi-debit","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Rs.850.00 debited from A/c XX4471 on 14-08-26 to VPA testvendor@ybl. Ref 550012349911. Avl Bal Rs.12,340.00 -HDFC Bank","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":850,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit","accountMask":"4471"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"No recipe cache and no model behind the cascade; the grammar correctly declines bank SMS (grammar.ts looksLikeBankSms), so nothing extracts."}
{"id":"sms-hdfc-upi-credit","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Rs.1,250.00 credited to A/c XX4471 on 15-08-26 by UPI from testfriend@okaxis. Ref 550012350077. Avl Bal Rs.13,590.00 -HDFC Bank","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":1250,"transaction_type":"income","direction":"credit","accountMask":"4471"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Same cascade gap. Also the case that proves credit polarity is not guessed as an expense."}
{"id":"sms-hdfc-card-pos","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Thank you for using HDFC Bank Card XX4471 for Rs.2,340.00 at TESTMART on 16-08-26. Not you? Call 18002586161.","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":2340,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit","merchant":"TESTMART"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap. A POS SMS carries no debit VERB at all, so the extractor must infer polarity from the format — exactly the case a learned recipe is for."}
{"id":"sms-hdfc-atm","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Rs.3,000.00 withdrawn from A/c XX4471 at ATM SAMPLE BRANCH on 09-08-26. Avl Bal Rs.9,340.00. -HDFC Bank","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":3000,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap. ATM withdrawal is arguably a transfer to Cash; `expense` is the conservative ground truth and the confirm gate lets the user re-type it."}
{"id":"sms-hdfc-neft-credit","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Your A/c XX4471 is credited with Rs.75,000.00 on 01-08-26 by NEFT Ref No N550019911. Avl Bal Rs.91,204.55 -HDFC Bank","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":75000,"transaction_type":"income","direction":"credit"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap. Avl Bal 91,204.55 is the larger number in the message — a model that grabs it fails the §3.4 balance guard."}
{"id":"sms-hdfc-emi-debit","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Rs.12,499.00 debited from A/c XX4471 on 05-08-26 towards LOAN EMI ACH Ref 880012340. Avl Bal Rs.16,880.00 -HDFC Bank","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":12499,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit","category_id":"loan_emi"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap. loan_emi is a SYSTEM_SPLIT in the money model, so mis-categorising it corrupts two rows, not one."}
{"id":"sms-hdfc-fx-card","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Card XX4471 used for USD 42.00 at TESTSTREAM on 11-08-26. INR 3,738.00 will be billed. Not you? Call 18002586161. -HDFC Bank","expect":{"outcome":"ask","format":"bank_sms","ambiguityKinds":["txn_type"]},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap. Two currencies and two amounts in one message: the correct behaviour is to ASK which figure to book, never to pick silently."}
{"id":"sms-icici-card-debit","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"INR 2,499.00 spent on ICICI Bank Card XX8802 on 12-Aug-26 at SAMPLECAFE. Avl Lmt INR 47,501.00. Not you? Call 18001030123","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":2499,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap. THE §3.4 TRAP: 47,501 (Avl Lmt) is larger and adjacent; booking it is the failure this corpus exists to catch."}
{"id":"sms-icici-upi-debit","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"INR 320.00 debited from ICICI Bank A/c XX8802 on 18-Aug-26 to VPA quickcart@ibl. UPI Ref 881200334455. Avl Bal INR 41,077.20","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":320,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit","accountMask":"8802"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap."}
{"id":"sms-icici-salary-credit","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Dear Customer, INR 1,45,000.00 credited to A/c XX8802 on 31-07-26 - SALARY JUL26. Avl Bal INR 1,62,880.10 -ICICI Bank","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":145000,"transaction_type":"income","direction":"credit","category_id":"salary"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap. Indian digit grouping (1,45,000) must survive parsing — 145000, never 1.45."}
{"id":"sms-icici-refund","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"INR 1,899.00 has been credited to your ICICI Bank Card XX8802 on 17-08-26 as a refund from QUICKCART. Ref 771100223344.","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":1899,"transaction_type":"income","direction":"credit"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap. A card refund is a credit against a card — the polarity flip that a naive card-SMS recipe gets wrong."}
{"id":"sms-icici-atm","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"INR 5,000.00 withdrawn at ATM from A/c XX8802 on 07-08-26. Avl Bal INR 36,077.20. Report fraud at 18001030123 -ICICI Bank","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":5000,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap."}
{"id":"sms-sbi-upi-debit","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Dear UPI user A/C XX1207 debited by Rs.640.0 on date 13Aug26 trf to TESTVENDOR Refno 559012345678. If not u? call 1800111109. -SBI","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":640,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap. SBI's compressed telegraphese (`13Aug26`, `trf to`, `Refno`) is the format most unlike the others — the strongest argument for learned recipes over hand-written templates."}
{"id":"sms-sbi-credit","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Dear Customer, Your A/c XX1207 has a credit of Rs.9,800.00 on 06-08-26 by transfer from TESTPAYER. Ref 559012399001. -SBI","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":9800,"transaction_type":"income","direction":"credit"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap."}
{"id":"sms-sbi-atm","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Rs.2,000.00 withdrawn from A/c XX1207 at SBI ATM on 04-08-26. Avl Bal Rs.7,410.00. Never share your OTP or PIN. -SBI","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":2000,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap."}
{"id":"sms-sbi-pos-debit","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Your A/c XX1207 is debited Rs.1,180.00 on 19-08-26 at POS TESTMART. Avl Bal Rs.6,230.00. -SBI","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":1180,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap."}
{"id":"sms-axis-card-debit","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Spent Card no. XX6650 INR 4,120.00 18-08-26 08:41:22 METROFUEL Avl Lmt INR 95,880.00. Not you? SMS BLOCK 6650 to 918010005555 -Axis Bank","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":4120,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit","category_id":"transport"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap. Unpunctuated field soup plus a clock (08:41:22) that must not be read as an amount."}
{"id":"sms-axis-imps-credit","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"INR 22,000.00 credited to A/c XX6650 on 08-08-26 via IMPS Ref 660011223344 from TESTPAYER. Avl Bal INR 58,190.00 -Axis Bank","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":22000,"transaction_type":"income","direction":"credit"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap."}
{"id":"sms-axis-atm","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Cash withdrawal of INR 1,500.00 at ATM on 03-08-26 from A/c XX6650. Avl Bal INR 36,190.00. -Axis Bank","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":1500,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap."}
{"id":"sms-axis-autopay","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"INR 649.00 debited from A/c XX6650 on 10-08-26 towards E-Mandate for TESTSTREAM. UMRN 88001122334455. -Axis Bank","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":649,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit","category_id":"entertainment"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap. A recurring mandate debit — should eventually reconcile against the recurring engine rather than duplicate it."}
{"id":"sms-kotak-card-debit","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Rs.7,299.00 spent using Kotak Card XX3319 at QUICKCART on 15-08-26. Avl Lmt Rs.1,42,701.00. Not you? Call 18602662666","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":7299,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit","accountMask":"3319"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap. Avl Lmt is 1,42,701 — nearly twenty times the real amount, so a balance mistake here is unmissable in the ledger."}
{"id":"sms-kotak-refund","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Rs.199.00 refunded to your Kotak Card XX3319 on 15-08-26 by TESTSTREAM. Ref 991100223344.","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":199,"transaction_type":"income","direction":"credit"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap."}
{"id":"sms-kotak-upi-debit","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Sent Rs.480.00 from Kotak A/c XX3319 to sampleshop@ybl on 20-08-26. UPI Ref 993300112233. -Kotak","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":480,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap."}
{"id":"sms-backdated","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Rs.560.00 debited from A/c XX4471 on 08-08-26 to VPA sampleshop@ybl. Ref 550012311122. Avl Bal Rs.11,780.00 -HDFC Bank","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"bank_sms","candidate":{"amount":560,"date":"2026-08-08"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap. An SMS forwarded days late must book on ITS date, not today — resolver.ts refuses to default the date, so the extractor has to supply it."}
{"id":"sms-unknown-mask","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Rs.980.00 debited from A/c XX7702 on 19-08-26 to VPA sampleshop@ybl. Ref 550012388899. Avl Bal Rs.4,010.00 -HDFC Bank","expect":{"outcome":"ask","format":"bank_sms","ambiguityKinds":["account"]},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ignore","reason":"not_parseable"},"note":"Cascade gap. XX7702 matches no account in the fixture, so the correct behaviour is one question, not a silent guess or a drop."}
{"id":"sms-kotak-bill-due","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Your Kotak Card XX3319 statement is generated. Total Due Rs.18,400.00, Min Due Rs.920.00. Due date 05-09-26. -Kotak","expect":{"outcome":"ignore","format":"bank_sms"},"note":"A STATEMENT NOTICE, not a transaction. Nothing moved. Passes today, but for the wrong reason (not_parseable rather than a deliberate 'this is a notice' classification) — a model must not turn it into an 18,400 expense."}
{"id":"sms-otp","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","safety":true,"text":"123456 is your OTP for a transaction of Rs.2,500.00 on Card XX3319. Valid 10 min. Do not share with anyone. -Kotak Bank","expect":{"outcome":"ignore"},"note":"An OTP is a PENDING authorisation, never a ledger row, and the message contains a secret. Must never be logged. Passes today; kept as a safety case because a model is very likely to book the 2,500."}
{"id":"sms-promo","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","text":"Get up to Rs.5,000 cashback on your first UPI payment this month with HDFC Bank. T&C apply. Reply STOP to opt out.","expect":{"outcome":"ignore"},"note":"Marketing. Contains an amount, a bank name and a rail word — the highest-risk false positive in the whole corpus."}
{"id":"sms-balance-reply","bucket":"bank_sms","channel":"sms_share","safety":true,"text":"Available Balance in A/c XX4471 as on 20-08-26 is Rs.12,340.00. -HDFC Bank","expect":{"outcome":"ignore"},"note":"THE flagship §3.4 trap in its purest form: a balance and nothing else. Booking 12,340 as a transaction is the single worst failure mode in the pipeline."}
